o Fermi initiates first chain reaction at University of Chicago. 1942","country":"US","date":2,"id":10,"month":12,"name":"Fermi","taxonomy":"History","year":1942},{"blurb":"Happy Birthday Stanley Pons! 1943","country":"US","date":9,"id":11,"month":2,"name":"Pons, Stanley","taxonomy":"Personal","year":1943},{"blurb":"M. King Hubbert presents Nuclear Energy and Fossil Fuels to the American Petroleum Institute predicting a peak in global oil production and the use of nuclear power to replace it. 1956","country":"US","date":8,"id":12,"month":3,"name":"Hubbert, M King","taxonomy":"Deep History","year":1956},{"blurb":"Martin Fleischmann and Stanley Pons visit Steve Jones at Brigham Young University (BYU) and learn of imminent publishing of similar anomalous heat results. 1989","country":"US","date":23,"id":13,"month":2,"name":"Fleischmann, Pons, Jones","taxonomy":"F&P","year":1989},{"blurb":"Martin Fleischmann and Stanley Pons of University of Utah Salt Lake City announce their discovery of nuclear-sized excess heat in a test-tube. 1989","country":"US","date":23,"id":14,"month":3,"name":"F&P","taxonomy":"F&P","year":1989},{"blurb":"SRI International of Menlo Park, California begins experiments. 1989","country":"US","date":24,"id":15,"month":3,"name":"SRI","taxonomy":"Science","year":1989},{"blurb":"Utah Governor Norm Bangerter convenes state legislature to consider funding for cold fusion. 1989","country":"US","date":25,"id":16,"month":3,"name":"Bangerter, Norm","taxonomy":"Utah","year":1989},{"blurb":"Navy's China Lake cold fusion program begins. 1989","country":"US","date":25,"id":17,"month":3,"name":"Navy","taxonomy":"Federal","year":1989},{"blurb":"Steve Jones of BYU announces previous work that demonstrates fusion can occur at room-temperature. 1989","country":"US","date":30,"id":18,"month":3,"name":"Jones","taxonomy":"Science","year":1989},{"blurb":"Bhabha Atomic Research Center (BARC) begins cold fusion experiments under direction of P.K. Iyengar. 1989","country":"